        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.582,
            0.048,
            0.86,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": "Exploring Some Geometric Themes"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.087,
            0.674,
            0.11
          ],
          "content": "？ What happens to the length of a line in its projection?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.113,
            0.588,
            0.169
          ],
          "content": "Let us consider projections in Fig. 4.3. For example let l be the actual length of the line and $p$ be the length of its projection."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.168,
            0.587,
            0.206
          ],
          "content": "Draw AE ⊥ BC. AECD is a rectangle (why?). So, $AE = DC = p.$ Also, $\\angle  AEB = 90^{\\circ}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.206,
            0.569,
            0.232
          ],
          "content": "Can you now compare the lengths p and l?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.244,
            0.588,
            0.285
          ],
          "content": "？ When is the length of the projected line equal to its actual length?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.629,
            0.09,
            0.841,
            0.288
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.705,
                0.281,
                0.761,
                0.297
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 4.3"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_19_image_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.299,
            0.801,
            0.34
          ],
          "content": "？ What do you think are the different possible projections of a square that we get based on its orientation?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.353,
            0.802,
            0.392
          ],
          "content": "？ What do you think is the projection of a parallelogram under different orientations?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.396,
            0.803,
            0.454
          ],
          "content": "Can this ever be a quadrilateral that is not a parallelogram? As a starting point, you could think about the projection of a pair of parallel lines."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.463,
            0.812,
            0.526
          ],
          "content": "? What can you say about the projection of an n-sided regular polygon? [**Hint:** Projection of a polygon is composed of the projections of its sides.]"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.818,
            0.456,
            0.904,
            0.518
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_19_image_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.536,
            0.556,
            0.557
          ],
          "content": "Let us consider projections of solids now."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.566,
            0.677,
            0.589
          ],
          "content": "？ How would the projections of a cube and a cone look?"
